# The prisoners in the dungeon cells (docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_larders.md §4, §5).
# nadia: Nadia Boteanu (docs/voice/nadia_boteanu.md), cell N1. doru: only if the party let him out of the undercroft
# (docs/voice/doru.md), cell N2. anatol: "Brother Anatol" (docs/voice/brother_anatol.md), a vampire spawn posing as a
# prisoner, cell S1. shawl: the prop at the servants' stair foot after Nadia ran alone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Nadia Boteanu

~ nadia
if flag.larders_nadia_fate == "waits"
-> nadia_waiting
endif
if not flag.larders_nadia_met
-> nadia_first
endif
Nadia Boteanu: You came back. Nobody comes back down here. Except the cook, and he doesn't count.
-> nadia_menu

~ nadia_first
set larders_nadia_met
quest the_cooks_guests found
Narrator: A young woman in a soot-streaked dress is chained by one ankle to a ring in the wall. She presses into the corner as the gate swings open.
Nadia Boteanu [afraid]: Don't. Please. Oh. You're not him. You're not the cook either.
Nadia Boteanu: Nadia. Nadia Boteanu. I light the lamps in Vallaki. Lit them. I don't know which, any more.
-> nadia_menu

~ nadia_menu
* How did you end up down here? -> nadia_taken
* [if not flag.larders_hall_told] Has anyone taken you out of this cell? -> nadia_hall
* [if not flag.larders_nadia_freed] Let's get that chain off you. -> nadia_chain
* [if flag.larders_nadia_freed] Now, how to get you out of the castle. -> nadia_way
* We'll be back. -> nadia_bye

~ nadia_taken
Nadia Boteanu: A carriage stopped beside me on the road at dusk. Black, no driver. The door swung open by itself.
Nadia Boteanu: I thought, well, it's going toward Vallaki, and my feet hurt. It was not going toward Vallaki.
interject tag:cheerful: Never get into the carriage with no driver. That's a rule now.
Nadia Boteanu [sad]: It should have been a rule already.
-> nadia_menu

~ nadia_hall
set larders_hall_told
Nadia Boteanu: Once. The cook walked me down the passage, past the other cells, to a long hall at the end.
Nadia Boteanu: A man sat at the head of a table made of bones. The chairs were bones. The lamp over it burned green.
Nadia Boteanu [afraid]: He asked me about Vallaki's lamps, very politely, as if he cared. Then he sent me back. He said I wasn't ripe.
interject class:rogue: The lamp. Did you see what fed it?
Nadia Boteanu: A chain went up into the dark toward the noise. There's a noise down here like something breathing, all the time.
-> nadia_menu

~ nadia_chain
Narrator: The shackle is old iron. Its chain runs to a ring bolted deep into the stone.
* [if flag.larders_keys_taken] (Use the jailers' keys.) -> nadia_unchained
* [Sleight of Hand DC 13] (Work the shackle's pin loose.) -> nadia_unchained | nadia_pick_fail
* [Athletics DC 15] (Wrench the ring out of the wall.) -> nadia_unchained | nadia_wrench_fail
* We'll find the keys and come back. -> nadia_menu

~ nadia_pick_fail
time +10
Narrator: The pin turns halfway and sticks. Ten minutes gone, and it will take another try.
-> nadia_chain

~ nadia_wrench_fail
time +10
Narrator: The ring grinds in its socket and holds. Somewhere above, something stops moving to listen, and then goes on.
-> nadia_chain

~ nadia_unchained
set larders_nadia_freed
quest the_cooks_guests freed
Narrator: The shackle opens. She rubs her ankle, stands, sits down again, and stands up properly the second time.
-> nadia_way

~ nadia_way
Nadia Boteanu: Out. Yes. Which way is out? I came in asleep.
* [if flag.larders_cyrus_helps] The cook will smuggle you out at dawn in his scrap barrel. Go to the kitchen. -> nadia_escape
* Up the servants' stair, through the castle and out the front door. Run, and don't stop. -> nadia_run
* Shut yourself in here and hide until we've finished with him. -> nadia_hide
* [if not flag.larders_cyrus_helps] Wait here a little. We'll find you a safer way. -> nadia_bye

~ nadia_escape
set larders_nadia_fate = "escaped"
quest the_cooks_guests escaped
Nadia Boteanu: In a barrel. With the scraps. Of course. Why would anything here be easy.
Narrator: She hugs the nearest of you, hard and quick, and goes up the passage toward the warm smell of the kitchen.
-> END

~ nadia_run
Nadia Boteanu [afraid]: Up there? Through his house? On my own?
interject tag:blunt: It's his house. Every corridor in it is his.
* Yes. Go now, while he's busy with us. -> nadia_run_go
* No, you're right. Not that way. -> nadia_way

~ nadia_run_go
set larders_nadia_fate = "sent_alone"
Narrator: She swallows, nods, and goes. You hear her bare feet on the stair for a long time, and then you don't.
-> END

~ nadia_hide
set larders_nadia_fate = "waits"
quest the_cooks_guests hidden
Nadia Boteanu: Hide. In the cell. Like a guest who's very good at being a guest. All right. Shut the gate. Come back.
-> END

~ nadia_waiting
Nadia Boteanu: Is it over? Is he gone?
* [if flag.larders_cyrus_helps] Not yet. But the cook will smuggle you out at dawn. Go to the kitchen. -> nadia_escape
* Up the stair now, and run. -> nadia_run
* Not yet. Stay hidden. -> END

~ nadia_bye
Nadia Boteanu [sad]: Shut the gate behind you. It's worse when it's open and I can't go anywhere.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Doru

~ doru
if not flag.larders_doru_met
-> doru_first
endif
Doru [sad]: Still here. Still hungry. Have you come to watch?
-> doru_menu

~ doru_first
set larders_doru_met
Narrator: A thin young man hangs in silvered chains, his toes just clear of the floor. His lips are cracked back to the gums. He knows you at once.
Doru: You. You opened the door under the church. I remember how you smelled. Rain and roads.
Doru [sad]: I went home to him, to the castle. I thought he'd give me a seat at the table. He gave me this, for coming back with nothing.
-> doru_menu

~ doru_menu
* Your father still prays for you, Doru. -> doru_father
* [if flag.doru_cure_promised] We promised your father we'd look for a cure. -> doru_cure
* We could end this, Doru. If you want it ended. -> doru_rest
* (Strike the chains off him.) -> doru_free
* We're leaving you here. -> doru_leave

~ doru_father
Doru: Does he? Still? Even now? Tell him... no. Don't tell him where I am. Tell him I went far away.
Doru [angry]: Come a little closer while you think it over. Just a little.
-> doru_menu

~ doru_cure
Doru: There isn't one. There's the hunger and there's the stake. I've asked the dark every night. That's all it says.
-> doru_menu

~ doru_rest
set larders_doru_fate = "rest"
Doru: Yes. Please. Before he wants me again.
interject class:cleric: Close your eyes, Doru. Think of the church with the candles lit.
Narrator: It is quick. The hunger goes out of his face, and for a moment he is only a tired boy. Then he is dust in the chains.
interject tag:devout: We'll tell his father he was brave at the end. It's even true.
-> END

~ doru_free
set larders_doru_fate = "freed"
Doru: Thank you. Thank you. Oh, you're warm. You're all so warm.
combat larders_doru_hunger

~ doru_leave
set larders_doru_fate = "left"
Doru [angry]: No. No! Come back! I'm better now! I'm better!
Narrator: He is still shouting it when the passage turns.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- "Brother Anatol"

~ anatol
if flag.larders_anatol_fate == "unmasked"
-> anatol_unmasked_again
endif
if not flag.larders_anatol_met
-> anatol_first
endif
Brother Anatol [smile]: Friends. Bless the dawn, you came back.
-> anatol_menu

~ anatol_first
set larders_anatol_met
Narrator: A man in a clean grey habit kneels in the straw with his hands folded. A sun is scratched into the wall above him. Beside him sits a tray of bread nobody has touched.
Brother Anatol [smile]: Bless the dawn. Visitors, and not the cook. The Morninglord heard me after all.
Brother Anatol: Brother Anatol, of St. Andral's in Vallaki. I came to pray for the lord of this house. He did not care for it.
-> anatol_menu

~ anatol_menu
* How long have you been down here? -> anatol_how
* [if flag.larders_anatol_noticed] Your breath doesn't fog in this cold, Brother. Ours does. -> anatol_unmask
* [Insight DC 15] (Watch him while he talks.) -> anatol_seen | anatol_insight_fail
* [if not flag.larders_anatol_prayed] [Religion DC 12] Pray the dawn prayer with us, Brother. -> anatol_prayer_wrong | anatol_prayer_passes
* [if flag.lucian_met] Father Lucian keeps St. Andral's with two acolytes. He never mentioned you. -> anatol_lucian
* [if flag.larders_anatol_warned] The cook says you never touch his soup. -> anatol_cook
* [Cleric] (Raise your holy symbol to the gate.) -> anatol_symbol
* [Paladin] (Raise your holy symbol to the gate.) -> anatol_symbol
* Come on, Brother. We're getting you out. -> anatol_free
* Stay quiet. We'll be back. -> END

~ anatol_how
set larders_anatol_noticed
Brother Anatol: Weeks. I count the days by the cook's visits. He brings bread. I pray over it and give it back.
Narrator: Your own breath hangs white in the cold of the cell while he talks. His doesn't.
-> anatol_menu

~ anatol_seen
Narrator: He talks about the dawn the way a man describes a country he has only read about. And he hasn't blinked once.
-> anatol_unmask

~ anatol_insight_fail
Narrator: He seems exactly what he says: a tired, frightened holy man, too gentle for this place.
-> anatol_menu

~ anatol_prayer_wrong
set larders_anatol_prayed
Narrator: He starts the prayer smoothly and then asks the dawn to wait. Every priest of the Morninglord asks it to come.
-> anatol_unmask

~ anatol_prayer_passes
set larders_anatol_prayed
Narrator: He murmurs along with you, eyes closed. If he stumbles, you can't hear it.
-> anatol_menu

~ anatol_lucian
Brother Anatol: Lucian. Yes. Of course. Lucian and I... It was a long time ago.
Narrator: Father Lucian is not much over forty.
-> anatol_unmask

~ anatol_cook
Brother Anatol: I fast. It is a discipline.
Narrator: Weeks of fasting, and his cheeks are fuller than yours.
-> anatol_unmask

~ anatol_symbol
Narrator: He looks at the holy symbol for exactly as long as a man can look at the sun. Then he looks at the floor, and keeps looking.
-> anatol_unmask

~ anatol_unmask
set larders_anatol_fate = "unmasked"
Narrator: The kindness goes out of his face all at once, like a lamp turned down. He stands, and the shackle slides off his wrist. It was never locked.
Brother Anatol [sly]: Pity. The Master so enjoys it when the rescuers walk me to his table themselves.
* Then we'll save him the trouble. -> anatol_fight
* Stay in your cell. We'll be back with a stake. -> anatol_left

~ anatol_fight
combat larders_false_brother_unmasked

~ anatol_left
Narrator: He laughs. He sits down in the straw again, folds his hands, and goes back to waiting.
-> END

~ anatol_unmasked_again
Brother Anatol [sly]: Back with that stake? Or did you only come to look at me?
* Back with the stake. -> anatol_fight
* Only to look. -> anatol_left

~ anatol_free
set larders_anatol_fate = "freed"
Narrator: He rises, thanking you in a low voice, and steps out into the passage behind you.
Brother Anatol [sly]: Bless you. Truly. Now hold still.
combat larders_false_brother

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- After Nadia ran alone

~ shawl
Narrator: A soot-streaked shawl lies on the bottom step, folded neatly, the way a servant folds things for the laundry.
if not flag.larders_nadia_lost
set larders_nadia_lost
quest the_cooks_guests caught
endif
interject tag:blunt: She got as far as the stair. Then someone folded her shawl.
-> END
